{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115920",
      "title": "Structural Directives & Syntactic Sugar",
      "lectureOrder": 161,
      "videoOrder": 153,
      "sourceHash": "876f9b9ed5241b445d4a96bfea672585337d59f4a0a0fbb54d79e51c47106a50",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.69,
          "end": 4.35,
          "en": "I did mention before that this asterisk here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.35,
          "end": 7.62,
          "en": "in front of a directive is syntactic sugar",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.62,
          "end": 9.213,
          "en": "for using NG template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.14,
          "end": 12.99,
          "en": "So instead of using NG template like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.99,
          "end": 15.33,
          "en": "you could also add your paragraph like that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.33,
          "end": 19.62,
          "en": "and add the app auth directive directly on it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.62,
          "end": 23.321,
          "en": "but now prefixed with this asterisk.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.321,
          "end": 27.87,
          "en": "Which is simply some special naming pattern Angular picks up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.87,
          "end": 30.42,
          "en": "and understands to under the hood",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.42,
          "end": 33.033,
          "en": "create such a NG template element instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.74,
          "end": 36.57,
          "en": "Now, what's important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.57,
          "end": 40.32,
          "en": "about this asterisk is that it will not just lead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.32,
          "end": 42.52,
          "en": "to NG template being added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.52,
          "end": 47.37,
          "en": "but that it will also automatically set up property binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.37,
          "end": 50.84,
          "en": "as if you were using square brackets here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.84,
          "end": 52.53,
          "en": "And therefore the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.53,
          "end": 54.9,
          "en": "between the quotes is now evaluated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.9,
          "end": 58.023,
          "en": "as TypeScript code instead of as a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.01,
          "end": 62.16,
          "en": "So here where I want to pass a hard coded string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.16,
          "end": 63.99,
          "en": "as a value for this input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.99,
          "end": 67.11,
          "en": "I therefore must wrap this with single quotes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.11,
          "end": 71.403,
          "en": "so that I do create a string value in TypeScript code again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.647,
          "end": 76.77,
          "en": "But with that, we can use this shorter syntax here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.77,
          "end": 79.953,
          "en": "to conditionally render this content here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.53,
          "end": 85.5,
          "en": "So with that, it still works as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 85.5,
          "end": 88.233,
          "en": "but now by using this shorter syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.242,
          "end": 93.12,
          "en": "And this also allows me to add some finishing touches here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 93.12,
          "end": 96.33,
          "en": "because I also prepared some CSS classes in advance,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.33,
          "end": 99.24000000000001,
          "en": "which have nothing to do with this directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.24000000000001,
          "end": 102.78,
          "en": "which are just there to make the app look a bit better.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.78,
          "end": 105.81,
          "en": "And therefore I'll add the protected dash content class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.81,
          "end": 107.61,
          "en": "to this paragraph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 107.61,
          "end": 111.221,
          "en": "And then here, give this a second class name of admin,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.221,
          "end": 114.36,
          "en": "and then I'll add a second paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.36,
          "end": 117.18299999999999,
          "en": "which should be rendered for regular users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 118.05,
          "end": 120.427,
          "en": "I'll set that as a value for app auth",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.86,
          "end": 126.28,
          "en": "and then replace the admin CSS class with unauthenticated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 127.398,
          "end": 131.73,
          "en": "and say regular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 131.73,
          "end": 134.103,
          "en": "users should see this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 136.05,
          "end": 137.31,
          "en": "And last but not least,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.31,
          "end": 142.31,
          "en": "I'll add a third paragraph for guest users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 144.54,
          "end": 147.88,
          "en": "where unauthenticated is replaced with authenticated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 149.28,
          "end": 152.043,
          "en": "and where I'll say, guest users should see this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 153.45,
          "end": 154.71,
          "en": "And now only one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 154.71,
          "end": 158.28,
          "en": "of those three paragraphs should be visible at a time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 158.28,
          "end": 161.703,
          "en": "depending on the user authentication status.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 162.66,
          "end": 165.69,
          "en": "Initially it's the guest user's paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 165.69,
          "end": 167.88,
          "en": "but if I log in as an admin",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 167.88,
          "end": 171.32999999999998,
          "en": "with the credentials you find in the auth service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 171.32999999999998,
          "end": 172.413,
          "en": "this changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 173.55,
          "end": 178.55,
          "en": "And if I log in as a user, this also changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 179.91,
          "end": 183.12,
          "en": "And that's how you can use your own structural Directives.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 183.12,
          "end": 185.913,
          "en": "And most importantly, this is how you can build them.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
